{"slug":"juiced-eliminator","title":"Juiced Eliminator","desc":"PSP, Juice Games / THQ 2006","notes":["The PSP version of Juiced, read from game.dat: the same .dat archives as the PC game, nested (cars/<car>.dat, carmesh.dat, cartextures.dat, scripts.dat).","The meshes are .ppm files (the PSP form of the PC .d8m: float vertices in triangle strips), the pictures are 8-bit palette pictures in the PSP swizzle.  Part trees, materials and the car list (cardefs.txt) are the PC formats: see ../Juiced/README.txt for how a car is put together (stock parts, wheels, kits, vinyls, rims).","GARAGE MODELS: the PSP keeps two sets of every car.  Race: cars/<car>.dat (the PC model reduced to about 55 % of the triangles, smaller pictures, no engine bay or underbody, flat rim faces).  Garage / menus: cars/<car>_ui.dat (the full car in one level of detail, the PC detail with the black cabin lining, engine bay, underbody, 3D rims, pictures twice the size).  The cars here are the garage ones (for the cars the PC game also has: the PC models with the PSP pictures; the cars new on the PSP exist only here).","Interior: as in the game's garage: no seats, a black lining (black2) and the inner window panes (<car>_INT) behind the tinted glass.","RIMS: the full garage rims are in the root of game.dat (mesh\\wheel_<name>.ppm, hash-named in the archive; named again and collected by juiced_psp_garage.py): bbs vs1-vs10 and oz vs1 19 (instead of their race versions), enkei vs1, evo8, konig vs1 / vs2, oz classe 19, rx7 and a set of OZ rims that are not in the shop list (named after their material: oz_antares, oz_chrono, oz_classe, oz_f1cup, oz_opera3_c, oz_operaiiis, oz_slegforg, oz_slegger_g / _s / _w, oz_vellaii, oz_volc; a hash in the name = another model with the same material), roja.  stock_<car> = the garage wheel of the car.  The other shop rims exist on the PSP only as race models (a rim lip plus a picture face, drawn as in the game); their full versions are in ../Juiced/_Rims.  _rims.csv says which is which (supplier 'garage only').","NEW ON THE PSP (not in the PC game): civic_si, clio_v6, coupe, ibiza, megane, mustang_05, scion (names in _car_names.csv). _Unused: c2, cobra and commodore, cars cut from the game (bodies without bumpers or wheels, not in the car list).","The archives store hashes instead of names: the names are the PC ones with .ppm for .d8m; the files of the new cars were named by the same patterns (juiced_psp_names.py).  About 1 triangle in 10 of the PSP bodies faces the other way in the files (the PSP draws them from both sides): turned to match the normals.","No _Vinyls folder: the vinyl pictures are the PC ones at a lower resolution (see ../Juiced/_Vinyls).","Strip junk: every PSP strip runs through several separate pieces, and the triangles between two pieces are not part of the car (streaks through the windows, sheets under the bumpers, stripes over the grilles, flat duplicates on the body).  The game does not draw them: the vertex format keeps the PS2 'ADC' bit (the integer 0x8000 instead of 1.0 in the w of the position) on every vertex whose triangle is skipped.  Those triangles are left out here (juiced_ppm.py; about 12 % of the strip triangles), so the meshes are exactly what the game draws."],"tags":["juiced-eliminator"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["3000gt","MITSUBISHI 3000 GT",3924989,"juiced-eliminator","car-3000gt.zip","thumbs/juiced-eliminator/cars/car-3000gt.webp"],["300zx","NISSAN 300ZX",4585939,"juiced-eliminator","car-300zx.zip","thumbs/juiced-eliminator/cars/car-300zx.webp"],["350z","NISSAN 350Z",3692578,"juiced-eliminator","car-350z.zip","thumbs/juiced-eliminator/cars/car-350z.webp"],["ac_integra","ACURA INTEGRA TYPE-R",4288655,"juiced-eliminator","car-ac_integra.zip","thumbs/juiced-eliminator/cars/car-ac_integra.webp"],["ac_nsx","ACURA NSX",2262637,"juiced-eliminator","car-ac_nsx.zip","thumbs/juiced-eliminator/cars/car-ac_nsx.webp"],["beetle","VOLKSWAGEN BEETLE 1.8T",2292893,"juiced-eliminator